// A `comptime assert` over a type's layout is answered by kama itself since KR-94: `sizeof(Vec4)` folds from the
// target's layout model, so the claim fails as an ordinary kama diagnostic — at `kama check` and in the editor, not
// only once the C compiler runs. (Before, an aggregate's layout went to C as a `_Static_assert` and this fixture
// sat in run_tests.sh's `analysis_skip`; the one layout C still answers is a `type extern value`'s,
// tests/xfail/comptime_assert_extern_layout.d.)
import { std::math::Vec4 };

comptime assert(cond: sizeof(Vec4) == 15, msg: "Vec4 is not 15 bytes");

fn int32 main() { return 0; }
